{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Relocation payment required only for lower income households displaced by demolition for new construction","requirement":"Only lower income households displaced by demolition of their units for new construction must receive a relocation payment; the payment must be consistent with the relocation benefits public entities pay under state law.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lower income households being displaced for the purpose of demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Demolition/new construction displacement in the City of Los Angeles"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 66300.6","quoted_span":"The City's Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO) and the State's Housing Crisis Act (HCA) require that ONLY lower income households being displaced for the purpose of demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction must receive relocation payment consistent  to the relocation benefits required to be paid by public entities pursuant to Chapter 16 (commencing with Section 7260) of Division 7 of Title 1 (Government Code 66300.6(b)(4)(A)).","interaction":"RSO or JCO amounts are the minimum; increased only if the state HCA or RPO requires it.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Deadline and method for paying relocation assistance","requirement":"The landlord must make relocation assistance available within 15 days of service of the written eviction notice, paying each tenant an equal pro rata share and the higher amount where more than one amount applies.","key_value":"15 days","coverage_conditions":"All rental units for which relocation assistance is required to be provided to tenants.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A tenant may raise the landlord's failure to provide relocation assistance as an affirmative defense in an action to recover possession, may file a complaint with LAHD, and may seek a private right of action.","effective_date":null,"citation":"RAC Regulations § 960.00","quoted_span":"4. Payments shall be made available within fifteen (15) days of service of the written notice of eviction; however, the landlord may, at the landlord's sole discretion and at the landlord's cost, elect to pay the monetary relocation benefits through an escrow account.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Single-family JCO relocation: one month's rent","requirement":"For a single-family dwelling subject to the JCO owned by a natural person with no more than four dwelling units, the landlord pays one month's rent in effect when the notice to terminate was served, as payment or credit.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Single-family dwellings subject to the JCO owned by a natural person, including a trust or registered legal entity controlled by that person, who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Single-family dwelling subject to the JCO, natural person owner"},"exemptions":"Los Angeles Municipal Code Section 151.30(E) does not apply.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC § 165.06","quoted_span":"Single Family Dwellings Owned by Natural Persons When the residential real property is a single-family dwelling subject to the JCO and the owner is a natural person, including natural persons who hold properties in a trust or registered legal entity controlled by that natural person, who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot in the City of Los Angeles: one month's rent that was in effect when the landlord served the written notice to terminate the tenancy, as either a monetary payment or credit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Relocation offset against accumulated rent","requirement":"A landlord may offset the tenant's accumulated rent against any relocation assistance, except where the assistance is owed because a governmental agency order requires the tenant to vacate or comply over an unpermitted dwelling.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Any relocation assistance payment owed to a tenant under the City's relocation rules.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"No offset where relocation assistance is owed because of a governmental agency order to vacate or comply issued for an unpermitted dwelling.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC § 151.09","quoted_span":"Relocation Offset: A landlord may offset the tenant's accumulated rent against any relocation assistance, unless the relocation assistance is owed because a termination of tenancy is required by a governmental agency order to vacate or comply issued for an unpermitted dwelling.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
